ICA Toolkit Android Plugin :
Device Plugin for GripID FAP30 Devices with Smartcard and Fingerprint Support.

This is a combi plugin for this device with Smartcard and Fingerprint Support.

Supported Android Application Binary Interfaces (ABIs):
	1. armeabi-v7a
	2. arm64-v8a

Contents:

  gripidfab30-plugin.aar
      Complete plugin — Java classes + all native libs bundled 
  device_filter.xml
      USB device filter — must be copied to res/xml/ in your app.

Installation:

  1. Copy gripidfab30-plugin.aar to your app module's libs/ directory.

     app/build.gradle:

         dependencies {
             implementation fileTree(dir: 'libs', include: ['*.aar', '*.jar'])
         }

  2. Copy device_filter.xml to app/src/main/res/xml/device_filter.xml.

     This file tells Android which USB devices to associate with your app
     when they are connected.

  3. Update AndroidManifest.xml:

     a) USB permission and hardware feature:

         <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.USB_HOST" />
         <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.usb.host" />

     b) Activity that handles card operations — must be exported for
        Android 12+ (API 31+):

         <activity
             android:name=".YourCardActivity"
             android:exported="true">
             <intent-filter>
                 <action android:name="android.hardware.usb.action.USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED" />
             </intent-filter>
             <meta-data
                 android:name="android.hardware.usb.action.USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED"
                 android:resource="@xml/device_filter" />
         </activity>

        Without android:exported="true", the USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED intent
        will not be delivered on Android 12+.


Notes:

  - Works with application context or Activity context.
  - Fingerprint capture is USB-based — no camera permission required.
  - Tested on arm64-v8a and armeabi-v7a devices running Android 8.0+.

NEW in v3.0.4.
